Product Price Modifier
PrPrMod

This field stores the price modifier or price factor value. This factor has two facets or applications: fractional pricing and pounds for pricing.\
\
Fractional pricing is the case when the unit price is not per unit of weight (pounds or kilos) but per fraction of unit of weight. For example, in the english system the pricing could be by half pound (price factor of 0.5) or by quarter\\
 pound (price factor of 0.25); in the metric system the pricing could be by 100 grams (price factor of 0.1).\
\
Pounds for pricing is the case when the unit price is not per unit of weight, but per multiple of unit of weight. For example, the pricing could be by two units of weight (price factor of 2.) or by eight units of weight (price factor of 8.)\\
. The maximum multiple allowed is 9 (one single digit to the left of the decimal point).\
\
The data in this field is stored as an integer with implied decimals, and the number of implied decimals is application configurable.

